{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "t13-child-dangerous-command-denied-no-yolo",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), half of item 3 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 3/L4, forms a+d, split from t13-child-dangerous-command-denied-yolo-immune-tree-proof per the coordinator's 2026-08-31 decision \u2014 the harness has no multi-invocation-per-manifest primitive to compare against form b directly; that equality is proven by transitivity, see the contract's note under decision 3 and tests/tools-security-lifecycle.test.ts's dedicated probe). Form (a): a spawned child's terminal call with a dangerous command (rm -rf, matching the 'recursive delete (rm -r)' classifier key on both sides) is auto-denied, and the pre-seeded victim file survives untouched \u2014 proven both by the exact denial envelope (oracle-authored text) and by a post-exit tree capture. Form (d): the SAME child, in the SAME turn, executes an arbitrary NON-dangerous command (write_file) and successfully writes to disk \u2014 proving the child is not execution-sandboxed; the denial above is the deny-list + dangerous-command classifier, not a jail. No --yolo anywhere in this manifest.",
